				"start": 0,
				"end": 255,
				"data": " A `//` in a whitespace-sensitive element's attribute list runs to end of line, so the `>`\n\ttakes its own line instead of hugging the last attribute. The break lands inside the tag,\n\twhere no character is content, so the literal text is untouched. "
